cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Paper 2: Beyond 'Magic Numbers' — A Threshold Justification Stack for Clinical AI Governance"
version: "1.0.0"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.19499798
message: "If you use this repository, please cite the accompanying BMJ Health & Care Informatics paper."
type: software
abstract: >
  Reproducibility repository for Paper 2 of the Ethical Alpha Audit research
  programme. The repository combines two scopes:

  (1) Framework-comparison work (notebooks 01–04): renders manuscript Tables 1–3
  (six structural failure mechanisms; TJS specification; framework comparison),
  TJS record schema demonstrations, and release validation. Existing scope
  through repository version 1.0.0.

  (2) Computational sensitivity analysis (notebooks 05–08, package
  ``tjs_sensitivity/``, added at WS-2.6 in 2026-05-03): models how variation
  in inter-rater agreement (κ) on the Negative Harm Test propagates to four
  governance outcomes under stated modelling assumptions. Three κ regimes
  (falsification κ<0.40, caution 0.40≤κ<0.60, operational κ≥0.60) are derived
  analytically from the simulation outputs.

  NON-VALIDATION DISCLAIMER for sensitivity work: the simulation is a
  computational sensitivity analysis under stated modelling assumptions; it
  does not validate the TJS framework empirically, does not estimate κ values
  for any real institutional setting, and does not substitute for human
  inter-rater validation. The κ tolerance regime is normative-from-analysis
  and is replaceable by empirical pilot data when available. See
  ``docs/sensitivity/non_validation_disclaimer.md`` for the full statement.
